// kyoten::frame::Pose — a position and an orientation, as an XR device's pose is (an OpenXR action space, located at a
// time): what a `Pose` action holds (components § Decided, step 5 question 6). Y up, right-handed, metres, as every
// position is, and in a zone, as every position is (components § Decided, question 9): `position` is the offset from
// `zone`'s centre, so a pose far from the origin keeps float32's precision (design/input.md § Decided, 2026-11-26).
// The cursor's ray through a view is the first device to bind one; an XR device's aim pose is the same shape.

import { std::math::Vec3, std::math::Quat, ZoneCoord };

export { Pose };

type value Pose {
    public ZoneCoord zone;
    public Vec3 position;
    public Quat orientation;

    // At the origin zone's centre, turned as the world is: what a pose action reads before any input.
    public default ctor identity() {
        this.zone = ZoneCoord.origin();
        this.position = Vec3.zero();
        this.orientation = Quat.identity();
    }
}
